-- תקנון שירות עובדי הוראה, פרק 3, §3.7 מחנך הכיתה
-- The class educator in the elementary school: who must take the post, the
-- educator's duties to the class, the parents and the school, the
-- prohibitions, the class-education allowance and the educator's hours.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT common

§ `3.7 מחנך הכיתה`

-- akn:chp_3__sec_3_7/p2 Table of contents: 3.7.3.
-- akn:chp_3__sec_3_7/p3 Table of contents: 3.7.6.1.
-- akn:chp_3__sec_3_7/p4 Table of contents: 3.7.6.2.

DECLARE `3.7 party` IS ONE OF
    `a takanon party` HAS `who` IS A Party

DECLARE `educator's act` IS ONE OF
    `shape the school by section 2 of the State Education Law`
    `accept the post of class educator`
    `see, with the class's teachers, to its studies and social life, teach it as one unit, bring its affairs before the principal and the teachers and foster ties with the parents`
    `guide the pupils in attendance, conduct, manners, punctuality, cleanliness and the school's rules and duties`
    `foster, with the class's teachers and the parents, the pupils' religious growth and understanding`
    `prepare the pupils for the festivals, memorial days and Independence Day from Torah sources`
    `guide the pupils in keeping the commandments outside school, involving the parents`
    `coordinate the class's teachers and set homework time per subject`
    `centralise and check the grades`
    `bring a grading dispute to the principal`
    `follow each pupil's development and give special care to the weak`
    `initiate parents' meetings with the subject teachers`
    `develop the class's social life and organise its institutions`
    `talk on national, social, current and cultural matters in educator's lessons`
    `invite each pupil's parents`
    `set a weekly time to receive parents and pupils`
    `tell the parents the reception time`
    `convene the class's parents`
    `know and visit the pupils' homes`
    `carry out the principal's and council's instructions and report`
    `handle the class's discipline`
    `follow the special rules for exceptional pupils`
    `keep the class diary and summarise lateness and absence`
    `prepare the material for the pedagogical council and the report cards`
    `keep the pupil card and complete it at year's end`
    `see to the pupils' appearance`
    `see to the classroom's appearance`
    `accept from pupils or parents a gift of benefit that is not a symbolic token of thanks`
    `give paid private lessons to pupils of her school` HAS `with the supervisor's approval` IS A BOOLEAN
    `teach organised school groups for pay` HAS `with the supervisor's leave` IS A BOOLEAN
    `smoke in the institution before the pupils while on duty`
    `publish in the press information on her work, post or institution, directly or through another, named or not, without leave of the director-general or his delegate`
    `write articles or publish books on her educational work, keeping confidentiality`
    `pass news of the institution to the spokesman through the district manager`

GIVEN `the act` IS AN `educator's act`, why IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC `3.7 party` `educator's act`
DECIDE `the educator must` `the act` why IS
    PARTY `a takanon party` `the teaching employee`
    MUST  a PROVIDED a EQUALS `the act`
    LEST  BREACH BY `a takanon party` `the teaching employee` BECAUSE why

GIVEN `the act` IS AN `educator's act`, why IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC `3.7 party` `educator's act`
DECIDE `the educator shall not` `the act` why IS
    PARTY `a takanon party` `the teaching employee`
    SHANT a PROVIDED a EQUALS `the act`
    LEST  BREACH BY `a takanon party` `the teaching employee` BECAUSE why

§§ `3.7.3 Duties`

@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_7__ssec_3_7_3__para_1 akn:chp_3__sec_3_7__ssec_3_7_3__para_1/p2
`3.7.3.1 shaping the school` MEANS
    `the educator must` `shape the school by section 2 of the State Education Law` "3.7.3.1: the educator shapes the school on the principles of section 2 of the State Education Law"

-- 2: every teacher accepts the post if asked; exempt is one teaching under
-- 10 lessons a week in the school, unless she teaches the class she would
-- educate "at least 6 to 8 lessons" (F-3.7-a). The reading adopted, as in
-- section 3.3: 6.
@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_7__ssec_3_7_3__para_2
GIVEN `lessons a week in the school` IS A NUMBER, `lessons in the class she would educate` IS A NUMBER, `asked` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `3.7 party` `educator's act`
DECIDE `3.7.3.2 accepting the post` `lessons a week in the school` `lessons in the class she would educate` `asked` IS
    IF `asked` AND NOT `exempt from the educator's post` `lessons a week in the school` `lessons in the class she would educate` 6
    THEN `the educator must` `accept the post of class educator` "3.7.3.2: a teacher asked to be a class educator accepts"
    ELSE FULFILLED

GIVEN `lessons a week in the school` IS A NUMBER, `lessons in the class she would educate` IS A NUMBER, threshold IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `exempt from the educator's post` `lessons a week in the school` `lessons in the class she would educate` threshold IF
    `lessons a week in the school` LESS THAN 10 AND `lessons in the class she would educate` LESS THAN threshold

`"at least 6 to 8 lessons" decides a teacher of 7 lessons both ways` MEANS
        NOT `exempt from the educator's post` 9 7 6
    AND `exempt from the educator's post` 9 7 8
#ASSERT `"at least 6 to 8 lessons" decides a teacher of 7 lessons both ways`

@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_7__ssec_3_7_3__para_3
GIVEN `full-time in two schools or more` IS A BOOLEAN, `this school has most of her hours` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may be made an educator in this school` `full-time in two schools or more` `this school has most of her hours` IF
    (NOT `full-time in two schools or more`) OR `this school has most of her hours`

@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_7__ssec_3_7_3__para_4
GIVEN classes IS A NUMBER, `teachers bound to educate` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a teacher may educate a second class` classes `teachers bound to educate` IF
    classes GREATER THAN `teachers bound to educate`

-- 5: in grades 1-2 one teacher, the educator, gives as a rule every lesson;
-- a departure needs the supervisor's approval; desirably also, where
-- possible, in grades 3-4 (checked, not required); from grade 5 the educator
-- is to teach her class as many lessons as possible.
@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_7__ssec_3_7_3__para_5
GIVEN grade IS A NUMBER
      `the educator teaches every lesson` IS A BOOLEAN
      `supervisor approved a departure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the educator teaches her class as many lessons as possible` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the lessons are rightly assigned` grade `the educator teaches every lesson` `supervisor approved a departure` `the educator teaches her class as many lessons as possible` IS
    IF grade AT MOST 2
    THEN `the educator teaches every lesson` OR `supervisor approved a departure`
    ELSE IF grade AT LEAST 5
         THEN `the educator teaches her class as many lessons as possible`
         ELSE TRUE

GIVEN grade IS A NUMBER, `the educator teaches every lesson` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `grades 3-4 as desired` grade `the educator teaches every lesson` IF
    (grade LESS THAN 3) OR (grade GREATER THAN 4) OR `the educator teaches every lesson`

@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_7__ssec_3_7_3__para_6
`3.7.3.6 the class's affairs` MEANS `the educator must` `see, with the class's teachers, to its studies and social life, teach it as one unit, bring its affairs before the principal and the teachers and foster ties with the parents` "3.7.3.6"

@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_7__ssec_3_7_3__para_7
`3.7.3.7 guidance` MEANS `the educator must` `guide the pupils in attendance, conduct, manners, punctuality, cleanliness and the school's rules and duties` "3.7.3.7"

-- 8: in a religious school, also religious growth, with (א) preparation for
-- festivals, memorial days and Independence Day from Torah sources and (ב)
-- guidance in keeping the commandments outside school, involving parents.
@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_7__ssec_3_7_3__para_8 akn:chp_3__sec_3_7__ssec_3_7_3__para_8__subpara_a akn:chp_3__sec_3_7__ssec_3_7_3__para_8__subpara_b
GIVEN `a religious school` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `3.7 party` `educator's act`
DECIDE `3.7.3.8 religious education` `a religious school` IS
    IF `a religious school`
    THEN `the educator must` `foster, with the class's teachers and the parents, the pupils' religious growth and understanding` "3.7.3.8: the educator in a religious school"
         RAND `the educator must` `prepare the pupils for the festivals, memorial days and Independence Day from Torah sources` "3.7.3.8א"
         RAND `the educator must` `guide the pupils in keeping the commandments outside school, involving the parents` "3.7.3.8ב"
    ELSE FULFILLED

@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_7__ssec_3_7_3__para_9
`3.7.3.9 coordinating the teachers` MEANS `the educator must` `coordinate the class's teachers and set homework time per subject` "3.7.3.9"

-- 10: the educator centralises the grades before each trimester and checks
-- them towards year's end; a dispute with a subject teacher goes, with the
-- principal, to the principal's decision, which the teacher may appeal to
-- the class's teachers.
@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_7__ssec_3_7_3__para_10
GIVEN `a grading dispute` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `3.7 party` `educator's act`
DECIDE `3.7.3.10 grades` `a grading dispute` IS
    `the educator must` `centralise and check the grades` "3.7.3.10"
    RAND (IF `a grading dispute`
          THEN `the educator must` `bring a grading dispute to the principal` "3.7.3.10: a grading dispute goes to the principal's decision"
          ELSE FULFILLED)

DECLARE `who decides a grading dispute` IS ONE OF `the principal`, `the class's teachers, on appeal`

GIVEN `the teacher appeals` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `who decides a grading dispute`
DECIDE `the last word on a grade` `the teacher appeals` IS
    IF `the teacher appeals` THEN `the class's teachers, on appeal` ELSE `the principal`

@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_7__ssec_3_7_3__para_11
`3.7.3.11 following each pupil` MEANS
    `the educator must` `follow each pupil's development and give special care to the weak` "3.7.3.11"
    RAND `the educator must` `initiate parents' meetings with the subject teachers` "3.7.3.11: the educator initiates parents' meetings with the subject teachers"

@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_7__ssec_3_7_3__para_12 akn:chp_3__sec_3_7__ssec_3_7_3__para_12__subpara_a
`3.7.3.12א social life` MEANS `the educator must` `develop the class's social life and organise its institutions` "3.7.3.12"

@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_7__ssec_3_7_3__para_12__subpara_b
GIVEN `a higher grade` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `3.7 party` `educator's act`
DECIDE `3.7.3.12ב educator's lessons` `a higher grade` IS
    IF `a higher grade`
    THEN `the educator must` `talk on national, social, current and cultural matters in educator's lessons` "3.7.3.12ב"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- 13: often, and at least once a trimester, each pupil's parents are invited.
-- Time in trimesters.
@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_7__ssec_3_7_3__para_13
GIVETH A DEONTIC `3.7 party` `educator's act`
DECIDE `3.7.3.13 inviting the parents` IS
    PARTY `a takanon party` `the teaching employee`
    MUST  `invite each pupil's parents`
    WITHIN 1
    LEST  BREACH BY `a takanon party` `the teaching employee` BECAUSE "3.7.3.13: each pupil's parents are invited at least once a trimester"

-- 14: a fixed weekly day and hour for parents and pupils, announced to the
-- parents at the start of the year; special appointments in exceptional
-- cases.
@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_7__ssec_3_7_3__para_14
`3.7.3.14 reception hour` MEANS
    `the educator must` `set a weekly time to receive parents and pupils` "3.7.3.14"
    RAND `the educator must` `tell the parents the reception time` "3.7.3.14: the parents are told at the start of the year"

-- 15: at least once a year the class's parents are convened. Time in years.
@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_7__ssec_3_7_3__para_15
GIVETH A DEONTIC `3.7 party` `educator's act`
DECIDE `3.7.3.15 the parents' meeting` IS
    PARTY `a takanon party` `the teaching employee`
    MUST  `convene the class's parents`
    WITHIN 1
    LEST  BREACH BY `a takanon party` `the teaching employee` BECAUSE "3.7.3.15: the class's parents meet at least once a year"

@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_7__ssec_3_7_3__para_16
`3.7.3.16 pupils' homes` MEANS `the educator must` `know and visit the pupils' homes` "3.7.3.16"

@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_7__ssec_3_7_3__para_17
`3.7.3.17 instructions and reports` MEANS `the educator must` `carry out the principal's and council's instructions and report` "3.7.3.17"

@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_7__ssec_3_7_3__para_18__subpara_a
`3.7.3.18א discipline` MEANS `the educator must` `handle the class's discipline` "3.7.3.18א"

@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_7__ssec_3_7_3__para_18__subpara_b
`3.7.3.18ב exceptional pupils` MEANS `the educator must` `follow the special rules for exceptional pupils` "3.7.3.18ב"

@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_7__ssec_3_7_3__para_19
`3.7.3.19 the class diary` MEANS `the educator must` `keep the class diary and summarise lateness and absence` "3.7.3.19"

@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_7__ssec_3_7_3__para_20
`3.7.3.20 the council and the report cards` MEANS `the educator must` `prepare the material for the pedagogical council and the report cards` "3.7.3.20"

@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_7__ssec_3_7_3__para_21 akn:chp_3__sec_3_7__ssec_3_7_3__para_21/p2
`3.7.3.21 the pupil card` MEANS `the educator must` `keep the pupil card and complete it at year's end` "3.7.3.21"

@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_7__ssec_3_7_3__para_22__subpara_a
`3.7.3.22א pupils' appearance` MEANS `the educator must` `see to the pupils' appearance` "3.7.3.22א"

@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_7__ssec_3_7_3__para_22__subpara_b
`3.7.3.22ב the classroom` MEANS `the educator must` `see to the classroom's appearance` "3.7.3.22ב"

@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_7__ssec_3_7_3__para_23
`3.7.3.23 gifts` MEANS `the educator shall not` `accept from pupils or parents a gift of benefit that is not a symbolic token of thanks` "3.7.3.23: no gifts of benefit, save symbolic ones"

-- 24א: no paid private lessons to pupils of her school — save as 24ב
-- allows: in a locality with one school, with the supervisor's approval.
@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_7__ssec_3_7_3__para_24__subpara_a
GIVEN `the only school in the locality` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `3.7 party` `educator's act`
DECIDE `3.7.3.24א private lessons` `the only school in the locality` IS
    PARTY `a takanon party` `the teaching employee`
    SHANT `give paid private lessons to pupils of her school` `the supervisor approved` PROVIDED (NOT `the only school in the locality`) OR (NOT `the supervisor approved`)
    LEST  BREACH BY `a takanon party` `the teaching employee` BECAUSE "3.7.3.24א: no paid private lessons to pupils of her school"

@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_7__ssec_3_7_3__para_24__subpara_b
GIVEN `the only school in the locality` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `3.7 party` `educator's act`
DECIDE `3.7.3.24ב the only school in the locality` `the only school in the locality` IS
    IF `the only school in the locality`
    THEN PARTY `a takanon party` `the teaching employee`
         MAY   `give paid private lessons to pupils of her school` `the supervisor approved` PROVIDED `the supervisor approved`
    ELSE FULFILLED

@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_7__ssec_3_7_3__para_24__subpara_c
GIVETH A DEONTIC `3.7 party` `educator's act`
DECIDE `3.7.3.24ג organised groups` IS
    PARTY `a takanon party` `the teaching employee`
    MAY   `teach organised school groups for pay` `the supervisor approved` PROVIDED `the supervisor approved`

@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_7__ssec_3_7_3__para_25__subpara_a
`3.7.3.25א smoking` MEANS `the educator shall not` `smoke in the institution before the pupils while on duty` "3.7.3.25א"

-- akn:chp_3__sec_3_7__ssec_3_7_3__para_25__subpara_b Points to the attached extension of the order against smoking in public places to educational institutions, a linked document not in this text.

@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_7__ssec_3_7_3__para_26__subpara_a
`3.7.3.26א the press` MEANS `the educator shall not` `publish in the press information on her work, post or institution, directly or through another, named or not, without leave of the director-general or his delegate` "3.7.3.26א: no publishing work matters in the press without the director-general's permission"

@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_7__ssec_3_7_3__para_26__subpara_b
GIVETH A DEONTIC `3.7 party` `educator's act`
DECIDE `3.7.3.26ב articles and books` IS
    PARTY `a takanon party` `the teaching employee`
    MAY   `write articles or publish books on her educational work, keeping confidentiality`

-- 26ג: an educator who thinks the public should hear of an important event
-- in the institution's life passes it through the district manager to the
-- spokesman's office, which publishes it as needed.
@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_7__ssec_3_7_3__para_26__subpara_c
GIVEN `thinks the public should hear of an event in the institution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `3.7 party` `educator's act`
DECIDE `3.7.3.26ג news of the institution` `thinks the public should hear of an event in the institution` IS
    IF `thinks the public should hear of an event in the institution`
    THEN `the educator must` `pass news of the institution to the spokesman through the district manager` "3.7.3.26ג: news goes through the district manager to the spokesman"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- akn:chp_3__sec_3_7__ssec_3_7_3/p1 The heading of the source list (אסמכתא).
-- akn:chp_3__sec_3_7__ssec_3_7_3/p2 A source: "post holders in the elementary school" (February 1975) and special director-general's circular ו' (5755).

§§ `3.7.6.1 Class-education allowance`

-- akn:chp_3__sec_3_7__ssec_3_7_6_1/p1 An amendment note: updated 21.7.02.

-- 1-3: 11.5% for educators of first grades (from 1.9.94), 10% for grades
-- 2-6 (from 1.1.01) and for grades 7-8 in elementary schools (from 1.6.95).
-- The base is section 1.12's: the combined salary (an input). Months are
-- year × 12 + month.
@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_7__ssec_3_7_6_1__para_1
GIVEN grade IS A NUMBER, `month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `class-education allowance rate` grade `month` IS
    BRANCH
        IF grade EQUALS 1 AND `month` AT LEAST 1994 TIMES 12 PLUS 9 THEN 0.115
    @ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_7__ssec_3_7_6_1__para_2
        IF grade AT LEAST 2 AND grade AT MOST 6 AND `month` AT LEAST 2001 TIMES 12 PLUS 1 THEN 0.10
    @ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_7__ssec_3_7_6_1__para_3
        IF grade AT LEAST 7 AND grade AT MOST 8 AND `month` AT LEAST 1995 TIMES 12 PLUS 6 THEN 0.10
        OTHERWISE 0

-- akn:chp_3__sec_3_7__ssec_3_7_6_1/p2 The heading of the source list (אסמכתא).
-- akn:chp_3__sec_3_7__ssec_3_7_6_1/p3 A source: collective agreement of 19.9.94.
-- akn:chp_3__sec_3_7__ssec_3_7_6_1/p4 A source: collective agreements of 8.9.98 and 10.7.02.
-- akn:chp_3__sec_3_7__ssec_3_7_6_1/p5 A source: summary of the committee of four of 19.9.95; special director-general's circular י' (5756).

§§ `3.7.6.1 The allowance`

-- The rate of 1-3 on the base: the combined salary (השכר המשולב), the base
-- section 1.12 uses, an input.
@export default The monthly class-education allowance of an elementary-school class educator under section 3.7.6.1 of the takanon
GIVEN grade IS A NUMBER @desc the grade of the class educated (1-8)
      `month` IS A NUMBER @desc the month, as year × 12 + month
      `combined salary` IS A NUMBER @desc the educator's combined salary (השכר המשולב), the base section 1.12 uses; an input
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `class-education allowance` grade `month` `combined salary` IS
    `combined salary` TIMES `class-education allowance rate` grade `month`

§§ `3.7.6.2 Educator's hours`

@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_7__ssec_3_7_6_2__para_1
GIVEN grade IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `educator's hours` grade IS
    IF grade AT LEAST 1 AND grade AT MOST 6 THEN 3 ELSE 0

-- 2: a principal, deputy or school coordinator who educates a class gets the
-- educator's hours as a teacher who educates one does, and they do not
-- reduce his minimum teaching hours.
@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_7__ssec_3_7_6_2__para_2
GIVEN grade IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `educator's hours of a principal, deputy or coordinator educating a class` grade IS
    `educator's hours` grade

GIVEN `minimum teaching hours of the post` IS A NUMBER, grade IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a manager-educator's minimum teaching hours` `minimum teaching hours of the post` grade IS
    `minimum teaching hours of the post`

-- akn:chp_3__sec_3_7__ssec_3_7_6_2/p1 The heading of the source list (אסמכתא).
-- akn:chp_3__sec_3_7__ssec_3_7_6_2/p2 A source: special director-general's circular ו' 5734, section 23.
-- akn:chp_3__sec_3_7__ssec_3_7_6_2/p3 A source: special director-general's circular ד' 5737, section 10.
-- akn:chp_3__sec_3_7__ssec_3_7_6_2/p4 A source: annex א to the special collective agreement of 16.11.83.
-- akn:chp_3__sec_3_7__ssec_3_7_6_2/p5 A source: director-general's circular מד/5.

-- Worked examples; the salary of 10,000 is a placeholder.
#ASSERT `class-education allowance` 1 (2002 TIMES 12 PLUS 3) 10000 EQUALS 1150
#ASSERT `class-education allowance` 4 (2002 TIMES 12 PLUS 3) 10000 EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT `class-education allowance` 4 (2000 TIMES 12 PLUS 3) 10000 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `educator's hours` 6 EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `a teacher may educate a second class` 12 10

#TRACE `3.7.3.13 inviting the parents` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a takanon party` `the teaching employee` DOES `invite each pupil's parents` AT 1
#TRACE `3.7.3.2 accepting the post` 9 7 TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a takanon party` `the teaching employee` DOES `accept the post of class educator` AT 0
